# Pin the working tree to LF.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. `tools/brand-provenance.txt` records the sha256 of the brand
# SVGs, of `palette.json` and of the two generated PNGs, and
# `uv run tools/gen_brand_raster.py --check` compares those hashes over raw bytes.
# Git on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every text file on checkout,
# which would change the bytes of each hashed source and fail the check for a
# contributor who changed nothing — the same flip-flop the hash pin replaced
# re-rendering to avoid. `.editorconfig` asks editors for LF; this asks git.
#
# Nothing is renormalised by adding this: no tracked file holds a carriage return,
# which `tools/tests/test_line_endings.py` keeps true.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch a binary's bytes, above all the two PNGs whose hashes are pinned.
*.png binary
